dcm2niix (Neurodesk app) third-party components

The Neurodesk dcm2niix application runs dcm2niix to convert images and curates
the result as BIDS. It uses the dcm2niix name with the permission of its author,
Chris Rorden (https://github.com/neurodesk/webapps/pull/382).

@niivue/dcm2niix 1.4.20261029 — BSD-2-Clause — https://github.com/niivue/niivue-dcm2niix
  WebAssembly build of dcm2niix v1.0.20261029 with OpenJPEG and CharLS.
dcm2niix — BSD licence below — https://github.com/rordenlab/dcm2niix
OpenJPEG — BSD-2-Clause, text below — https://github.com/uclouvain/openjpeg
CharLS — BSD-3-Clause, text below — https://github.com/team-charls/charls
miniz — public domain (Unlicense) — https://github.com/richgel999/miniz
nifti1_io — public domain — https://nifti.nimh.nih.gov
fflate 0.8.2 — MIT, Copyright (c) 2023 Arjun Barrett — https://github.com/101arrowz/fflate
@neurodesk/mri2vid DICOM reader — BSD-3-Clause, Copyright (c) 2023 Thom Shaw
  (packages/mri2vid/LICENSE)

Example data: series VS-SEG-001 of Vestibular-Schwannoma-SEG, The Cancer Imaging
Archive, CC BY 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/), unchanged.
Shapey J, et al. (2021) https://doi.org/10.7937/TCIA.9YTJ-5Q73 and
Scientific Data 8:286, https://doi.org/10.1038/s41597-021-01064-w.

